            <ArticleTitle>Trifurcation stenting using two guide catheters.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>636-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccd.22284</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Trifurcating coronary artery disease is a complex atherosclerotic process involving the origin of one or more of three side branches arising from a main trunk. The approach to treat trifurcation lesions has not been standardized. We describe a technique to percutaneously treat this lesion using routine day-to-day hardware and a unique two guide catheter technique.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
